    "body": "> What is the use case here, something which referenceTarget doesn't already cover?\n\n`referencetarget` allows referencing into shadowr oots it doesn't allow referencing out of them. So this covers the same scenarios as say the `.commandForElement` property does. Notably here cases where you have buttons or other form controls that you want inside of a shadowroot but that you also want to behave correctly is the key thing.\n\nAs for `form.elements` and how we handle retargeting that's an open question. We could either just retarget each one individually and ignore duplicates, or we could run it through a \"set\" step so that duplicates are removed. I don't have a solid leaning one way or the other.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
