    "body": "I've been thinking on this some more and I do think that a separate property is actually cleaner. .form remains and returns the form owner. .formElement simply does the element reflection behaviour that plays into the form owner machinery. There's situations where .formElement will return null (there's no attribute) but where .form does return a form element.",
