    "body": "One main question left seems to be around what to do regarding the `form.elements` property.\n\nAs currently defined I believe that `form.elements` would exclude any shadowed form controls (not even including retargeted host elements).\n\n> The [collection](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-collection) then represents a view of the subtree rooted at the [collection’s](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-collection) root, containing only nodes that match the given filter.\n\nIt's unfortunately not super well defined but the rooted word here is what I think is doing the heavy lifting? Claude seems to agree that collections don't currently include shadow root contents.\n\nRegardless of how collections are defined we have to decide what we want the API behaviour to be then we can worry about how to implement that desire.\n\n- Should form.elements include *any* entries associated with controls that are in a descendent shadow tree?\n- If so, those will need to be retargeted, should we exclude duplicates if two elements retarget to the same host?\n- What do we do about RadioNodeList's value getter/setter, we presumably would want it to actually work to change the value of inner radio inputs?\n\nGiven how collections are currently defined excluding any entries would be the easiest to specify, but we should work around that if we need to.\n\nMy two cents is that form.elements is probably not very useful as an API if you have shadow roots involved. Even if we included entries for the shadow hosts you can't use that to do anything useful, and existing code is more likely to get confused.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
