    "body": "> But form submission is precisely where you get the clashes and where it matters the most. It doesn't strike me as a principled design.\n\nMy understanding is that Shadow DOM is about encapsulating (to varying levels depending on open or closed) the children from the outside world, rather than the outside world from the children?\n\nA custom element today could exist using purely light dom, contain an input that then clashes with another form control.\n\nCan you help me understand how the encapsulation of shadow DOM as a design principle is a factor here?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
