    "body": "> But form submission is precisely where you get the clashes and where it matters the most. It doesn't strike me as a principled design.\n\nYeah, I get what you're saying and I agree with the concern.  It definitely could be a foot gun to do it carelessly, but at the same time it seems that there are sometimes reasons to do it, and the outer page can be manipulated easily already.  It just seems that there are really lot of elements which are just wrappers around their native counterpart which don't semantically change it in any meaningful way, they just add hooks for styling and things in a way they don't want the outer page to mess with or have to repeat - and those cases currently require handling _way too many things_.  Maybe this isn't right shape either, idk, but I think we have to solve those cases simply somehow.",
